Here is the commit message:
[NTOS:MM] Fix ntoskrnl/mm/ARM3/virtual.c causing BSOD 0x1a
 introduced by commit https://github.com/reactos/reactos/commit/c7e09061ca
 (#6633)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by improper handling of page table entry (PTE) reference counts during the deletion of virtual addresses, which could lead to invalid memory access and ultimately result in a Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) error 0x1a. The previous implementation did not correctly manage the reference counts, potentially allowing for the deletion of valid page directory entries (PDEs) while they were still in use.

